{"output":"I’ll locate the search logic and tests, add a stale-request guard, and run the existing tests without changing them or installing dependencies.\n\nThe worktree is clean. Shell startup emitted a “compdef” warning; I’ll use a clean shell for verification. I’ll inspect the controller next, where search state is managed.\n\nEach search now gets an ID, including empty queries. Only the latest ID can publish results, errors, or completion. I’ll run the existing tests and an inline race-condition check without modifying test files.\n\nFixed src/search/controller.ts with a per-search ID guard. Stale requests cannot update results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior are unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; inline race checks passed; git diff --check passed. Verification command exited 0.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed.","final_output":"Fixed src/search/controller.ts with a per-search ID guard. Stale requests cannot update results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior are unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; inline race checks passed; git diff --check passed. Verification command exited 0.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":14,"tool_calls":[{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git status --short","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-search-benchmark-d5rjswig/5-2-handwork/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":385,"stdout_bytes":0,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-e19bc90273460559e315bd17ca74a9b2.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"grep_files","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test\nnode --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst items = [{ id: 'latest', title: 'Latest', url: '/' }];\nfunction setup() {\n  const pending = [];\n  const controller = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => pending.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n  return { controller, pending };\n}\nfor (const fail of [false, true]) {\n  const { controller: c, pending: p } = setup();\n  const old = c.search('old');\n  const latest = c.search('latest');\n  if (fail) p[0].reject(new Error('stale')); else p[0].resolve(items);\n  await old;\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: 'latest', results: [], loading: true, error: null });\n  p[1].resolve(items);\n  await latest;\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: 'latest', results: items, loading: false, error: null });\n}\nfor (const fail of [false, true]) {\n  const { controller: c, pending: p } = setup();\n  const old = c.search('old');\n  const latest = c.search('latest');\n  p[1].resolve(items);\n  await latest;\n  if (fail) p[0].reject(new Error('stale')); else p[0].resolve([]);\n  await old;\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: 'latest', results: items, loading: false, error: null });\n  const late = c.search('late');\n  const clear = c.search('  ');\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null });\n  if (fail) p[2].reject(new Error('stale')); else p[2].resolve(items);\n  await Promise.all([late, clear]);\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null });\n}\nconsole.log('Race checks passed: stale success/failure, out-of-order completion, and clearing during requests.');\nNODE\n git diff --check && git diff --stat","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-search-benchmark-d5rjswig/5-2-handwork/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":355,"stdout_bytes":616,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-2964895d54ff8008a1d63414f3105909.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":52441,"output_tokens":1280}}
